    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a master service agreement for a new raw material supplier we're looking at for our Munich facility. Can you give me a checklist of standard terms and conditions I should include to protect us against supply chain volatility and sudden price fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely. For handling supply chain volatility, include terms about:\n\n1. Delivery commitments - minimum and maximum quantity, schedule.\n2. Cancellation and notice periods - conditions under which either party can cancel or modify the contract.\n3. Force Majeure - clause to protect against unforeseeable events impacting the supply chain.\n\nFor price fluctuations, consider terms such as:\n\n1. Fixed vs. variable pricing models - define how prices are calculated and when they can change.\n2. Price adjustment mechanisms - establish a clear formula or basis for price revisions.\n3. Hedging options - the opportunity for the buyer/seller to engage in price hedging.\n4. Price review periods - regular intervals at which agreed pricing adjustments can be made.",
